Open a file, then zerox it until all NL=5 layers are occupied and attempt one
more. The sixth duplicate finds no free layer slot, exercising findl's "no free
slot" return. Each zerox selects "zerox" from the button-3 menu, presses button 3
over the topmost (file) window to pick the source, then sweeps the new window's
rectangle, so every duplicate is of the same file and stacks another layer.

-- file --
hello world
second line
third line
